// Appending one chain segment to the body it continues.
//
// The seam is recorded inline, as a node of kind "chain" pushed between the
// segments, rather than in a table beside the function: a boundary is a
// property of the body, and keeping it there means every walk that already
// has the body has the seam too. The marker performs no action (count.id's
// stmt_actions) and emits nothing.

chain_tail(int[] pos, int[] params, int[] restated, int[] body) {
  chain_same(pos, params, restated);
  int[] seg = parse_block(pos);
  chain_add(body, seg);
} return void;
